WEBVTT

00:00:02.715 --> 00:00:06.605
Spec Studio is a Mac app for spec-driven development with Claude Code.

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:12.607
Each spec gets its own Claude session, and goes through five stages, from a spec to reviewed pull requests.

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:23.395
Add a repo, and its specs show in the sidebar, each with its stage and whose turn it is.

00:00:23.395 --> 00:00:29.511
Beside it are the reader, which shows the spec's documents, and the spec's Claude session, a real terminal.

00:00:35.316 --> 00:00:40.326
Make a spec with a title and a few sentences about what the user sees when it is done.

00:00:40.326 --> 00:00:41.491
Then choose a mode.

00:00:41.491 --> 00:00:45.918
Autopilot goes to reviewed draft pull requests with no question in between.

00:00:45.918 --> 00:00:49.763
Guided interviews you, and stops for your approval at each stage.

00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:52.034
Loop takes one small change at a time.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:03.790
In Spec, Claude writes the spec: a summary, the scope, and requirements with Given, When, Then scenarios.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.127
The reader shows each document as Claude writes it.

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:13.717
In Plan, Claude studies the code.

00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:19.527
It writes the approach, the repos that change, the steps, and a test for each scenario.

00:01:26.028 --> 00:01:29.321
In Build, Claude works in its own worktree and branch.

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:33.103
It commits each step, pushes, and opens a draft pull request.

00:01:33.103 --> 00:01:36.152
The Changes section shows each file and its diff.

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.097
Each spec also has a shell in its worktree.

00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:45.317
Run the tests, the app or git there.

00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:50.177
The studio command works in any terminal: here it lists the specs that need you.

00:01:55.007 --> 00:01:59.225
In Check, a self review reads each pull request with parallel finders.

00:01:59.225 --> 00:02:03.924
Three verifiers vote on each finding, and a finding needs two of three votes.

00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:06.093
Here, round one found two problems.

00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:08.985
Claude fixed both, and round two found nothing.

00:02:14.326 --> 00:02:16.944
The strip at the top says whose turn it is.

00:02:16.944 --> 00:02:21.388
The Priority panel lists the specs that need you, across all your repos.

00:02:21.388 --> 00:02:27.051
In Merge, Claude works through the reviewers' comments with you, and merges when you say so.

00:02:33.645 --> 00:02:36.360
Put your repos in areas, each with its color.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.496
Fold an area, and it shows how many specs need you.

00:02:39.496 --> 00:02:45.348
A project collects specs from many repos, with milestones, and a spec can wait for another spec.

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:55.054
Choose the colors of the app and its terminals from the Ghostty themes, light or dark.

00:02:59.001 --> 00:03:00.803
Install Spec Studio with Homebrew.

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:03.506
The guides on the site take you through each step.
